{"completed": true, "response": "<escape>{\n  \"report_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"judge_supported\": \"partly\",\n  \"report_quotes\": [\n    \"We recorded subthalamic local field potentials synchronized to gait kinematics in the medication-OFF and stimulation-Off state in 13 Parkinson’s disease patients with freezing of gait.\",\n    \"The aim of this study was to characterize the subthalamic signature of freezing while turning. STN-LFPs synchronized to gait kinematics in the medication-OFF and stimulation-Off state of 13 PwPD with FoG were recorded.\",\n    \"In summary, we demonstrate that freezing while turning is marked by frequency-specific abnormalities that emerge prior to freezing onset, most prominently impaired low beta desynchronization that persists throughout freezing episodes and may be suggestive of impaired supraspinal-motor integration during turning.\"\n  ],\n  \"judge_quotes\": [\n    \"Posted Date: May 6th, 2026\",\n    \"DOI: https://doi.org/10.21203/rs.3.rs-9617843/v1\",\n    \"Research Article\",\n    \"Supplementary material is available at NPJ Parkinson’s Disease online.\"\n  ],\n  \"why\": \"论文明确支持该研究由Philipp Klocke等作者开展，研究对象为13名帕金森病患者，报告所描述的研究规模及主要结论有原文依据。论文首页显示Research Square格式的DOI和Posted Date，支持该版本属于Research Square发布的研究稿件；摘要及讨论结论没有明确标注预印本身份。不过，附件只有论文全文，没有报告正文，因此无法独立核实报告第3.2节和第5.6节是否确实如指控者所述，没有将预印本状态与这项研究明确关联。指控者的描述有部分依据：DOI和发布日期支持其关于Research Square版本的判断，但全文没有直接声明该稿件未经同行评审或尚未正式发表。此外，原文还写有补充材料可在NPJ Parkinson’s Disease在线获取，这使得仅凭全文无法完全确定该研究是否不存在正式发表的同行评审版本。因此，两项说法均有部分依据，不能据此认定报告对13人研究的科学结果存在实质性误读；争议主要在于预印本身份及证据成熟度的标注是否充分。\"\n}</escape>", "metadata": {"session_handle": "4f069078-cafd-4d5b-b9fb-1ffb6a323364", "session_revision": 0, "session_ttl_max_hours": 6, "job_directory": "D:\\musicclaude\\gpt2agent-safechain\\runs\\gpt4\\pro-bridge-20261113T125244670884Z", "elapsed_seconds": 127.172, "completed_utc": "2026-11-13T12:54:51.841002+00:00", "model": "gpt-6-thinking", "thinking_effort": "max", "temporary": true, "unpersonalized": true, "gen